{
  "tier": "sweep",
  "description": "Option sweep, part F: curl and wget (no network on either side: usage and error paths only),\nand the `sh` / `bash` commands' own options.\n\nTransfers go to 127.0.0.1 port 1, which refuses on both sides, or to a name under `.invalid`,\nwhich never resolves; their diagnostics carry timings, so those cases compare the status and\nanything written to stdout or files. Error paths fold GNU's curly quotes into ASCII ones.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "opt curl: no url",
      "script": "{ curl; } 2>/tmp/err; echo \"status=$?\"; sed \"s/[‘’]/'/g\" /tmp/err",
      "tags": [
        "cmd.curl",
        "cmd.curl.error",
        "error"
      ],
      "options": {}
    },
    {
